pearance on The Voice, he made a key decision. He could not go on as he had before, privately managing demons while publicly presenting a cool head. It was time to speak out about the crippling mental health issue that had dogged his life, since teenagehood. Me and My Mate Jeffrey is the result: an honest, gripping read about living with depression and anxiety, and learning to manage it; about the crippling journey to finally acknowledging 'Jeffrey' - a foul-weather friend and unlikely motivator, who provided his own roadmap to a way forward; and about the mistakes Bressie made when he first came to a crossroads in his mental health journey, and decided, wrongly, he could manage it alone.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10406691-L.jpg","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":false,"publicFame":8,"criticalRenown":10,"controversy":3,"llmAffinity":74,"affinityResidual":4.76,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.12,"criticalRenown":0.12,"controversy":0.12,"llmAffinity":0.83},"tags":{"craft":"voice","evidence":"personal-experience","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Acknowledging and speaking openly about depression and anxiety, rather than managing them alone, can provide a path toward recovery.","confidence":0.96},"academicOrientation":{"score":18,"confidence":0.97},"profileConfidence":0.98,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"9217bf0677ca28b851c9f10edf063d2fae85ddee7dba70ec3a850af8d40a9daa","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"Niall Breslin's life changed in 2012 when, in the aftermath of a massive panic attack that hit him minutes before a live television appearance on The Voice, he made a key decision. He could not go on as he had before, privately managing demons while publicly presenting a cool head. It was time to speak out about the crippling mental health issue that